    66→Structured JSON logs for parsing by tools like Datadog, CloudWatch, etc.:\n    67→```bash\n    68→export LOG_FORMAT=json\n    69→bun run start:server\n    70→```\n    71→\n    72→Output example:\n    73→```json\n    74→{\"timestamp\":\"2025-01-06T10:30:45.123Z\",\"level\":\"info\",\"message\":\"API request\",\"tools\":[\"addTodo\",\"deleteTodo\"],\"messageCount\":3}\n    75→{\"timestamp\":\"2025-01-06T10:30:45.456Z\",\"level\":\"info\",\"message\":\"Tool calls\",\"toolCount\":1,\"tools\":[{\"name\":\"addTodo\",\"input\":{\"text\":\"groceries\"}}]}\n    76→```\n    77→\n    78→### Build\n    79→\n    80→Build all packages:\n    81→```bash\n    82→bun run build\n    83→```\n    84→\n    85→Build individual packages:\n    86→```bash\n    87→bun run build:client\n    88→bun run build:server\n    89→```\n    90→\n    91→## Packages\n    92→\n    93→### @use-ai/client\n    94→\n    95→React hooks library for AI integrations using WebMCP (Model Context Protocol). Features:\n    96→- `UseAIProvider` context component for WebSocket connection configuration\n    97→- Built-in floating AI chat UI (optional) - just enable with `showFloatingChat={true}`\n    98→- `useAI` hook that accepts tool definitions for AI agent function calling\n    99→- Automatic tool execution and result streaming\n   100→- Beautiful, responsive chat interface with message history\n   101→\n   102→### @use-ai/server\n   103→\n   104→WebSocket server that hosts AI agents and proxies requests to Claude API. Features:\n   105→- WebSocket-based client communication\n   106→- MCP tool registration and execution\n   107→- Conversation history management\n   108→- Claude API integration\n   109→- Dual-mode logging (pretty for development, JSON for production)\n   110→\n   111→### example\n   112→\n   113→An AI-powered todo list application demonstrating the use-ai library. The AI can:\n   114→- Add, delete, and toggle todos via natural language\n   115→- Query the current todo list\n   116→- Understand context and perform multiple operations\n   117→\n   118→## Tech Stack\n   119→\n   120→- **Runtime**: Bun\n   121→- **Language**: TypeScript\n   122→- **UI Framework**: React\n   123→- **AI Model**: Claude (Anthropic)\n   124→- **Protocol**: WebSocket + WebMCP\n   125→- **Build Tool**: Bun bundler\n   126→\n   127→## Usage Examples\n   128→\n   129→### Floating AI Chat (Recommended)\n   130→\n   131→The easiest way to add AI capabilities is using the built-in floating chat UI:\n   132→\n   133→```tsx\n   134→import { UseAIProvider } from '@use-ai/client';\n   135→import App from './App';\n   136→import { todoTools } from './tools';\n   137→\n   138→<UseAIProvider\n   139→  serverUrl=\"ws://localhost:8080\"\n   140→  showFloatingChat={true}\n   141→  globalTools={todoTools}\n   142→>\n   143→  <App />\n   144→</UseAIProvider>\n   145→```\n   146→\n   147→This displays a floating \"AI\" button in the bottom-right corner. Users can click it to open a chat interface and interact with your app using natural language.\n   148→\n   149→### Programmatic API\n   150→\n   151→For custom UI implementations:\n   152→\n   153→```tsx\n   154→import { UseAIProvider, useAI } from '@use-ai/client';\n   155→\n   156→function App() {\n   157→  const { response, loading, generate } = useAI({\n   158→    tools: {\n   159→      addTodo: {\n   160→        fn: (input) => addTodo(input.text),\n   161→        config: {\n   162→          description: 'Add a new todo item',\n   163→          parameters: {\n   164→            text: { type: 'string', required: true }\n   165→          }\n   166→        }\n   167→      }\n   168→    }\n   169→  });\n   170→\n   171→  return (\n   172→    <div>\n   173→      <button onClick={() => generate('Add a todo for grocery shopping')}>\n   174→        Ask AI\n   175→      </button>\n   176→      {response && <p>{response}</p>}\n   177→    </div>\n   178→  );\n   179→}\n   180→\n   181→<UseAIProvider serverUrl=\"ws://localhost:8080\">\n   182→  <App />\n   